{
    "method": "core.identityProviderConfigsCreatePrepare",
    "toolName": "identity-provider-configs-create-prepare",
    "operationId": "identity_provider_configs_create",
    "title": "Create an identity provider configuration (prepare)",
    "category": "Core",
    "description": "Step 1 of 2 for create identity provider configuration. Validates the arguments and returns a signed confirmation_hash plus a message to surface to the user. The user must reply with the literal word \"confirm\" before you call the matching -execute tool with the hash. Original action: Create an organization identity provider configuration for SAML, OIDC, SCIM, or XAA (ID-JAG). Set `config_scope` to `saml`, `oidc`, `scim`, or `xaa`. Use `domain_scope: selected` with `organization_domain_ids` to link specific organization domains, or `domain_scope: all` to cover all verified organization domains. SAML uses `saml_entity_id`, `saml_acs_url`, and `saml_x509_cert`; OIDC uses `oidc_issuer_url`, `oidc_client_id`, and `oidc_client_secret`; SCIM can be enabled with `scim_enabled`; XAA uses `id_jag_issuer_url` with optional JWKS and allowed-client settings. The create call requires explicit user confirmation before execution.",
    "requiredScopes": ["organization:write"],
    "annotations": {
